# Handover log

Shared log (both computers): `HANDOVER.md` at the root of `danson117/danson117.github.io` on **GitHub**. Not local-only. Not in Supabase. Covers HX, Life OS, Alpha_Learn, Karson_Learn, and any work the other computer must know. Visible rule: `HX/hx-rules.html` §1.

## Before editing

Read `HANDOVER.md` first. If the other computer logged work this PC does not have yet: pull GitHub `main` first; for Supabase / Vercel follow the log. Do not guess. Do not overwrite with an older local file.

## After every change

In the **same turn**, append key points to `HANDOVER.md` (date, which computer, what changed, where: GitHub / Supabase / Vercel), then commit and push. The user may switch to the other computer at any time; that machine must know what was done so it does not fall out of sync.

No force-push. No secrets. Do not write Supabase public table `hx_test`. Do not put staff-level training detail in the public log.

Computer role: `C:\Cursor_Work\MACHINE.md` on this PC only (do not commit). If missing, ask once which computer this is. Never store "this PC is the company computer" in a synced user rule.

## Live vs backup

Live site = **Vercel**. Data = **Supabase**. GitHub HTML = **backup only** (Pages need not stay current). Shared settings/records that should look the same on every device go to Supabase. Exception: HX permission gate (e.g. Training One View) — view vs edit may differ by unlock; board data still syncs via locked Edge.
